---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import Carousel from "./Carousel.astro";
import { links } from "../data/site";

import cutestCat from "../assets/img/poncho_cutest_cat.png";
import whatWereDoing from "../assets/img/poncho_what_were_doing.png";
import forThePeople from "../assets/img/poncho_for_the_people.png";

const pictureProps = {
  widths: [250, 350, 700],
  sizes: "(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 250px, 350px",
  formats: ["avif"] as "avif"[],
  fallbackFormat: "webp" as const,
  loading: "lazy" as const,
};
---

<section class="about background--blue-dark" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="section-inner reveal">
    <h2 class="text-align-center" id="about-title">About</h2>
    <div class="container">
      <Carousel label="About Poncho">
        <article class="lore">
          <Picture src={cutestCat} alt="Poncho" {...pictureProps} />
          <div class="lore__text">
            <h3>Cutest Cat on Base</h3>
            <p>Poncho is welcoming. Poncho is friendly. Poncho is cute. Poncho has mainstream appeal.</p>
            <p>
              There are no strings attached to Poncho. He is not related to anyone, he is not anyone’s cat, he is simply a
              cute cat wearing a poncho. Nothing needs to be said beyond, “I think that cat is cute.” And that is what we
              want — simplicity.
            </p>
            <button class="button button--blue" type="button" data-open-buy>Buy Now</button>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="lore">
          <Picture src={whatWereDoing} alt="Poncho" {...pictureProps} />
          <div class="lore__text">
            <h3>What We’re Doing</h3>
            <p>
              What we are striving to do is very straightforward: making things easy. A new crypto denizen’s foray into the
              space will be buying Poncho and joining a welcoming, active community of helpful individuals.
            </p>
            <p>
              Beyond that, we have some incredibly innovative ideas to help bring everyone on-chain. Poncho is
              family-friendly, so it only makes sense. These ideas are in the planning stages right now, but expect to hear
              more in due time!
            </p>
            <a class="button button--blue" href={links.telegram} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join Community</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="lore">
          <Picture src={forThePeople} alt="Poncho" {...pictureProps} />
          <div class="lore__text">
            <h3>For The People</h3>
            <p>
              As you can see, Poncho is for the people. Poncho is everyone’s cat. And he’s wearing a poncho. He’s here to
              help, and with the help of Base, his dreams are achievable.
            </p>
            <p>So, come be a part of the <strong>#PonchoPals</strong>, and join Poncho on his journey to the stars!</p>
            <a class="button button--blue" href={links.forThePeople} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the Story</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </Carousel>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  @use "../styles/tools" as *;

  .lore {
    align-items: center;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--poncho_blue) 0%, var(--poncho_blue_dark) 40%);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    display: flex;
    padding: 30px;
    width: 100%;

    :global(img) {
      border-radius: 5px;
      display: block;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      margin: 30px;
      max-width: 350px;
    }
  }

  .lore__text {
    padding: 30px;

    .button {
      margin-top: 15px;
    }
  }

  @include media("xl") {
    .lore :global(img) {
      max-width: 250px;
    }
  }

  @include media("lg") {
    .lore {
      background: none;
      flex-direction: column;
      padding: 0;
      text-align: center;

      :global(img) {
        margin: 0 0 20px;
        max-width: 100%;
        width: 100%;
      }
    }

    .lore__text {
      padding: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
